### Setting up the project ###

1. Create a virtual environment using ```virtualenv nameofenv``` or ```python3 -m venv nameofenv```.
If you do not have virtualenv or venv installed, follow these links to set them up on your pc
    - https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/installing-using-pip-and-virtual-environments/#installing-virtualenv for windows
    - https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/installing-using-pip-and-virtual-environments/#installing-virtualenv for Unix/macOS

2. Activate the virtual environment using ```source nameofenv/bin/activate``` for linux and ```nameofenv\Scripts\activate``` for windows

3. Run ```pip install -r requirements.txt``` or ```pip3 install -r requirements.txt``` to install libraries and packages

4. Create a file in the "config" folder called <.env>
    - If you do not have postgres, follow these links to set it up:
        -Windows: https://www.prisma.io/dataguide/postgresql/setting-up-a-local-postgresql-database#setting-up-postgresql-on-windows
        -MacOs: https://www.prisma.io/dataguide/postgresql/setting-up-a-local-postgresql-database#setting-up-postgresql-on-macos
        -Linux: https://www.prisma.io/dataguide/postgresql/setting-up-a-local-postgresql-database#setting-up-postgresql-on-linux

    - Follow these links to create a database in Postgres:
        -Windows: https://blog.devart.com/create-database-in-postgresql.html
        -MacOs: https://www.codementor.io/@engineerapart/getting-started-with-postgresql-on-mac-osx-are8jcopb#b1-create-database-with-psql
        -Linux: https://www.liquidweb.com/kb/creating-and-deleting-a-postgresql-database/
    - Copy the content of env.example file into your .env file.
    - Follow this link to generate a secret key https://djecrety.ir/
    - Update the rest of the variables.

5. Run ```python manage.py migrate``` or ```python3 manage.py migrate``` to install new fields into the database.

6. Run ```python manage.py runserver``` or <python3 manage.py runserver>.
Your app is up!

7. To run tests, run ```python manage.py test ``` or ```python3 manage.py test```